Devel::Cover 1.52 merges runs in creation order using one-second timestamps
(lib/Devel/Cover/DB.pm, merge_runs). change.t rewrites its source between two
runs, so a half-second delay allows the runs to sort in the wrong order.
Wait longer than one timestamp tick. Keep every assertion and runtime source.
Original upstream Perl license notices remain intact.

--- a/tests/change.t
+++ b/tests/change.t
@@ -48 +48,3 @@
-    delay_after_run => 0.50,
+    # merge_runs orders databases by whole seconds; changed source versions
+    # must not share that timestamp, regardless of process ID ordering.
+    delay_after_run => 1.10,
